                    <packagedElement xmi:type="uml:Class" xmi:id="b75d85d7-f95b-4a8b-acbe-e7c3b5927ff4" name="ORB" isAbstract="true">
                      <ownedComment xmi:id="958a5615-2c4a-4635-8eaf-3afd2461f639" body="This ORB class is defined to provide a home for the&#xA;register_initial_reference operation, which is added by&#xA;portable interceptors and CORBA 2.4.  It is added here&#xA;until there is an official Java language mapping for the&#xA;method.&#xA;" annotatedElement="b75d85d7-f95b-4a8b-acbe-e7c3b5927ff4"/>
                      <generalization xmi:id="2b6119c2-e0f5-425c-96ea-86ebfac74849" isSubstitutable="true" general="8225a530-3a36-4dbf-a635-f750adb5f81f"/>
                    </packagedElement>
                  </packagedElement>
                </packagedElement>
              </packagedElement>
              <packagedElement xmi:type="uml:Package" xmi:id="e9fad4e2-0af1-4664-9e4f-7f066aee8359" name="pept">
                <packagedElement xmi:type="uml:Package" xmi:id="6b458370-1f5e-4364-b9b4-c36c3f88f2f6" name="broker">
                  <packagedElement xmi:type="uml:Interface" xmi:id="67897c39-c990-47b0-ae6f-427b497c3324" name="Broker" isAbstract="true">
                    <ownedComment xmi:id="881893fd-7608-4ba2-9bca-0a8fb83d65d3" body="@author Harold Carr&#xA;" annotatedElement="67897c39-c990-47b0-ae6f-427b497c3324"/>
                  </packagedElement>
                </packagedElement>
                <packagedElement xmi:type="uml:Package" xmi:id="88936306-23ba-4e3b-a813-97e4f2d5c58c" name="encoding">
                  <packagedElement xmi:type="uml:Interface" xmi:id="3040c844-9f2f-452e-b41e-c050494a7ac7" name="InputObject" isAbstract="true">
                    <ownedComment xmi:id="fb40f490-758f-4933-a60c-040f259949aa" body="&lt;p> An &lt;code>InputObject&lt;/code> is the interface used by the&#xA;presentation block to get programming language typed data from data&#xA;encoded in a message. &lt;/p>&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p> The implementation of an &lt;code>InputObject&lt;/code> contains the&#xA;encoded data.  When the presentation block asks for data the&#xA;implementation of &lt;code>InputObject&lt;/code> is responsible for converting&#xA;the encoded representation of the data to the types expected by the&#xA;programming language.&lt;/p>&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p>A particular &lt;em>encoding&lt;/em> would subclass&#xA;&lt;code>InputObject&lt;/code>.  The subclass would provide methods to get&#xA;the data types appropriate to the presentation block (e.g., simple&#xA;types such as int or boolean, all the way to any type derived from&#xA;&lt;code>java.io.Serializable&lt;/code>.).&lt;/p>&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p>Note: the protocol block may also use the &lt;code>InputObject&lt;/code> to&#xA;obtain header metadata.&lt;/p>&#xA;&#xA;@author Harold Carr&#xA;" annotatedElement="3040c844-9f2f-452e-b41e-c050494a7ac7"/>
                  </packagedElement>
                  <packagedElement xmi:type="uml:Interface" xmi:id="331e31ce-2680-4e39-b54a-d5cb5b555a2a" name="OutputObject" isAbstract="true">
                    <ownedComment xmi:id="011f2cc0-ffc9-4685-a668-4146841ddcff" body="&lt;p> An &lt;code>OutputObject&lt;/code> is the interface used by the&#xA;presentation block to give programming language typed data to&#xA;the encoding block to be encoded and sent in a message. &lt;/p>&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p> The implementation of an &lt;code>OutputObject&lt;/code> contains the&#xA;encoded data.  When the presentation block gives programming language&#xA;typed data to&#xA;&lt;code>OutputObject&lt;/code>, the&#xA;implementation of &lt;code>OutputObject&lt;/code> is responsible for converting&#xA;that data to the encoded representation of the data for a particular&#xA;encoding.&lt;/p>&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p>A particular &lt;em>encoding&lt;/em> would subclass&#xA;&lt;code>OutputObject&lt;/code>.  The subclass would provide methods to set&#xA;the data types appropriate to the presentation block (e.g., simple&#xA;types such as int or boolean, all the way to any type derived from&#xA;&lt;code>java.io.Serializable&lt;/code>.).&lt;/p>&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p>Note: the protocol block may also use the &lt;code>OutputObject&lt;/code> to&#xA;set header metadata.&lt;/p>&#xA;&#xA;@author Harold Carr&#xA;" annotatedElement="331e31ce-2680-4e39-b54a-d5cb5b555a2a"/>
                  </packagedElement>
                </packagedElement>
                <packagedElement xmi:type="uml:Package" xmi:id="905cd153-aa0f-4803-aa2e-702701449777" name="protocol">
                  <packagedElement xmi:type="uml:Interface" xmi:id="4a3e76d8-a809-4918-9439-6ebd9fc7c0e5" name="ClientDelegate" isAbstract="true">
                    <ownedComment xmi:id="29714800-5720-428a-8e8c-cbba9bf9588c" body="&lt;p>The presentation block interacts with the PEPt architecture&#xA;via the &lt;code>ClientDelegate&lt;/code>.&lt;/p>&#xA;&#xA;@author Harold Carr&#xA;" annotatedElement="4a3e76d8-a809-4918-9439-6ebd9fc7c0e5"/>
                  </packagedElement>
                  <packagedElement xmi:type="uml:Interface" xmi:id="9189d27b-a018-4684-b2d3-00b9440b853b" name="ClientInvocationInfo" isAbstract="true">
                    <ownedComment xmi:id="087f6e4f-7503-4ac4-a5fb-bb4ce2fc1dfc" body="@author Harold Carr&#xA;" annotatedElement="9189d27b-a018-4684-b2d3-00b9440b853b"/>
                  </packagedElement>
                  <packagedElement xmi:type="uml:Interface" xmi:id="d41367d8-24c5-471c-934b-67a9a6cb6ecd" name="ClientRequestDispatcher" isAbstract="true">
                    <ownedComment xmi:id="2cf9b7b2-31a7-4b14-aff0-41c176f65810" body="&lt;code>ClientRequestDispatcher&lt;/code> coordinates the request (and possible&#xA;response) processing for a specific &lt;em>protocol&lt;/em>.&#xA;&#xA;@author Harold Carr&#xA;" annotatedElement="d41367d8-24c5-471c-934b-67a9a6cb6ecd"/>
                  </packagedElement>
                  <packagedElement xmi:type="uml:Interface" xmi:id="3562b55c-a332-4789-8c12-564ddfd6e620" name="MessageMediator" isAbstract="true">
                    <ownedComment xmi:id="e58682a2-69e2-46ea-b44e-d2d490198f6d" body="&lt;code>MessageMediator&lt;/code> is a central repository for artifacts&#xA;associated with an individual message.&#xA;&#xA;@author Harold Carr&#xA;" annotatedElement="3562b55c-a332-4789-8c12-564ddfd6e620"/>
                  </packagedElement>
                  <packagedElement xmi:type="uml:Interface" xmi:id="307ef632-d762-4dc0-b0cb-c86f64c17d23" name="ProtocolHandler" isAbstract="true">
                    <ownedComment xmi:id="673a01b9-fa48-4f2c-a5b3-55204dfa91c3" body="&lt;code>ProtocolHandler&lt;/code> is used to determine the&#xA;type of an incoming message.&#xA;&#xA;@author Harold Carr&#xA;" annotatedElement="307ef632-d762-4dc0-b0cb-c86f64c17d23"/>
                  </packagedElement>
                  <packagedElement xmi:type="uml:Interface" xmi:id="cd707ead-fa4c-4c9b-a4ac-8402aa2ceea5" name="ServerRequestDispatcher" isAbstract="true">
                    <ownedComment xmi:id="b1e2b23d-9292-40a5-b797-6c6f80dea229" body="&lt;code>ServerRequestDispatcher&lt;/code> coordinates the request (and possible&#xA;response) processing for a specific &lt;em>protocol&lt;/em>.&#xA;@author Harold Carr&#xA;" annotatedElement="cd707ead-fa4c-4c9b-a4ac-8402aa2ceea5"/>
                  </packagedElement>
                </packagedElement>
                <packagedElement xmi:type="uml:Package" xmi:id="bae07060-9236-4174-92b2-40e1fc2baf62" name="transport">
                  <packagedElement xmi:type="uml:Interface" xmi:id="dfd5b043-0ae4-4ff2-b64c-b33274817a82" name="Acceptor" isAbstract="true">
                    <ownedComment xmi:id="cf570134-4658-48cc-ab2d-f9be34f2e22c" body="&lt;p>The &lt;b>&lt;em>primary&lt;/em>&lt;/b> PEPt server-side plug-in point and enabler&#xA;for &lt;b>&lt;em>altenate encodings, protocols and transports&lt;/em>&lt;/b>.&lt;/p>&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p>&lt;code>Acceptor&lt;/code> is a &lt;em>factory&lt;/em> for client-side&#xA;artifacts used to receive a message (and possibly send a response).&lt;/p>&#xA;&#xA;@author Harold Carr&#xA;" annotatedElement="dfd5b043-0ae4-4ff2-b64c-b33274817a82"/>
                  </packagedElement>
                  <packagedElement xmi:type="uml:Interface" xmi:id="f4127937-9727-447f-8d25-95798cf990b5" name="ByteBufferPool" isAbstract="true">
